<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kolomna</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kolomna is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, near the confluence of the Moskva and Oka rivers, about 110 kilometres south-east of Moscow. First mentioned in 1177, it belonged to the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryazan">Ryazan</a> until Daniel of Moscow seized it around 1301, giving Moscow control of the lower Moskva. Its brick kremlin, built in the 1520s, guarded Muscovy's southern frontier against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> raids.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kolomna.jpg" alt="Kolomna" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ghirlandajo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kremlin_Kolomna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
